cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use aberrant in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "aberrant: real-time anomaly detection for data streams"
type: software
abstract: >-
  aberrant is a typed Python library for unsupervised anomaly detection on
  data streams. Its detectors score each event as it arrives and update
  incrementally, covering isolation forests, distance and density methods,
  projection sketches, graph-edge detectors, time-series discords, online
  SVMs and reconstruction models, together with online preprocessing, drift
  detection, score thresholds and prequential evaluation.
